<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Anglo-Mysore War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1767">1767</a>–<a href="/years/1769">1769</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a> War (1767–1769) was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyder-ali">Hyder Ali</a>'s Mysore and the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a>, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizam-of-hyderabad">Nizam of Hyderabad</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> drawn in at different stages. After Hyder's cavalry raided close to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chennai">Madras</a>, the Company accepted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-madras">Treaty of Madras</a> of 1769, which restored conquests on both sides and promised mutual aid. The war established Mysore as the leading rival to British power in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-anglo-mysore-war.jpg" alt="First Anglo-Mysore War" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Miljoshi · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anglo-Mysore_War_1_and_2.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
